Z||000000||85fierogt||08-25-2001||05:40 PM||||ok guys im considering the ocelot performance exhaust from the fiero store, i would like to go flow but i dont have the money right now and i need to get this car on the road i bought it and from the cat out is all rusted out with holes so i searched and found that many people say that the ocelot exhuast rusts really easy in like a year so i was owndering if i bought some undecoating spray and sprayed the exhaust pipes would this solve the rust problem or would the undercoating not be able to take the heat inthat case if i sprayed it with a high heat tolerant paint would that again solve the rust problem if i kept up with it and would there be any perofrmance side effects with this? , thanks im new to all the exhaust stuff<BR>-brad||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||08-25-2001||05:47 PM||||The undercoating tends to be not much more than Roofing Tar. When the exhaust heats up, it WILL catch fire, or at least smoke badly, and burn off. Leaving you with no coating.<P>The only thing I could think of is coating the entire mess with high-temp manifold paint, before you install. That should protect it a little. <P>Of course, you COULD just do what I do to protect against rust: Wash the car WEEKLY. That includes an under-body blast. That'll keep salt/grit etc. from building up. ||||reg||12
Z||000002||85fierogt||08-25-2001||05:58 PM||||how exaclty do u blast the underbody its so freakin low?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||08-25-2001||06:47 PM||||2 ways:<BR>1) In the wand wash, just jam the wand underneath at an angle up, and hose. Blast out the wheelwells, and the susp. components. Not much will stick to the floorpan in the middle, so I don't worry too much about it. If you've ever been under the car, it's easy to see where dirt will collect, and 99% of the area is accessible with a wand. That's the HARD way.<P>2) The easy way is to go to most automatic car-washes. Almost all of the new touchless ones have an underbody wash. Do that every now and then. You don't have to worry too much during the summer. A large puddle will knock most of the dirt off. In the winter, I'd do it every couple of weeks, with a thourough wand wash every  other week. It's part of the car-maintenance.||||reg||7
